<title>GERMANY: Buba - Euro conversion rates should be set spring 98.</title>
<headline>Buba - Euro conversion rates should be set spring 98.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer said on Thursday that he expected a decision this year on how conversion rates for the euro single currency should be set.</p>
<p>He also said that no decision had yet been reached on how the rates would be established.</p>
<p>&quot;We in the Bundesbank would prefer that member states orientate towards conversion as simultaneously as possible,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said it could be sensible to indicate in the spring of 1998 what the conversion rates will be, and said the Bundesbank would discuss this subject in the next few months.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer was speaking at a news conference after a regular policy-setting council meeting.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
